| `tests/integration/test_banned_api_gate.py` | Walks the Python syntax trees from `tests/source_tree.py` and fails literal `getattr` calls on imported modules or wildcard imports that expose an API banned by `pyproject.toml`, unless a TID251 suppression gives a reason; a blank suppression reason, empty policy or empty tree fails too. | `make test` | — | Dynamic names and unrelated objects are outside this check. Not for ordinary imports or attribute access: ruff's TID251 rule judges those under `make lint`. | [python-style.md](../guides/python-style.md) | always |
